    "news": {
      "added": [
        {
          "id": 3431,
          "title": "Call for Participants in the Certificate Authority Technical Community and Kick-off Announcement",
          "announcement": "<p>The National Information Assurance Partnership/Common Criteria Evaluation and Validation Scheme (NIAP/CCEVS) is pleased to invite interested parties to be part of a Technical Community (TC) for the update of the Protection Profile for Certificate Authority (CA), Version 3.0.</p>\r\n<p>The purpose of this update is to:</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>Transition to the latest version of the Common Criteria, CC:2022;</li>\r\n<li>Align with the X.509 Functional Package;</li>\r\n<li>Modernize requirements; and</li>\r\n<li>Incorporate applicable Technical Decisions (TDs).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The CA TC kick-off meeting will be held on <strong>Thursday, October 15th, from 1300-1400 EDT</strong>. A meeting invitation will be sent to the TC alias.</p>\r\n<p>Additional Information:</p>\r\n<p>- All interested parties should apply to the CA TC by navigating to the <a href=\"https://www.niap-ccevs.org/technical-communities\">Technical Communities page</a>&nbsp;on the NIAP website and click \"Become A US Technical Community Participant\".</p>\r\n<p>- If you are already a member of the CA TC, there is no need to re-apply.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thank you for your interest and we look forward to your participation.</p>",
          "types": "1",
          "subject": null,
          "posted": "2026-09-11T10:32:11.500000Z",
